from lesson_data import P, S, E, Q, finish
LESSON=finish(dict(number=4,prereqs=[1,3],lead=P("Use logic, sets, relations, proof and probability to state what a program means and justify its claims.","用逻辑、集合、关系、证明与概率表达程序含义并论证结论。"),before=P("Know functions and loops. No previous proof course is assumed. ∀ means for every; ∃ means there exists.","了解函数与循环，无需证明课程基础。∀ 表示任意，∃ 表示存在。"),outcomes=[P("Build truth tables.","构建真值表。"),P("Use sets and relations.","使用集合与关系。"),P("Distinguish functions and injectivity.","区分函数与单射性。"),P("Construct induction proofs.","构造归纳证明。"),P("Compute finite conditional probabilities.","计算有限条件概率。")],
sections=[
S("Logic and quantifiers","逻辑与量词","<p>A proposition is a statement with a truth value. Negation flips it; conjunction requires both inputs; disjunction requires at least one. Implication p→q means not p or q: it is false only when p is true and q is false. This models a promise: when the precondition holds, the postcondition must hold. It is not a claim that p causes q. Quantifiers extend statements: every record has an ID differs from some record has an ID. Negating ∀x P(x) gives ∃x not P(x); one counterexample defeats a universal claim.</p>","<p>命题具有真值。否定翻转真值，合取要求双方成立，析取要求至少一方成立。蕴含 p→q 等价于非 p 或 q，仅在 p 真而 q 假时为假。它表达前置条件成立时后置条件必须成立，并不表示因果。每条记录都有 ID 与某条记录有 ID 不同。∀x P(x) 的否定是 ∃x 非 P(x)，一个反例即可推翻全称断言。</p>","When is p→q false?","p→q 何时为假？","Only when p is true and q is false.","仅 p 真、q 假时。"),
S("Sets and relations","集合与关系","<p>A set contains distinct elements without positional order. Union collects elements in either set; intersection keeps elements in both; difference A−B keeps elements only in A. A relation is a set of ordered pairs: borrowed_by can relate a book ID to a member ID. Reflexive means each element relates to itself; symmetric means each related pair reverses; transitive means xRy and yRz imply xRz. Equality has all three properties. A directed dependency relation need not be symmetric.</p>","<p>集合包含不同元素，不具有位置顺序。并集包含任一集合中的元素，交集保留共同元素，差集 A−B 保留仅在 A 中的元素。关系是有序对的集合，例如借阅关系连接书 ID 与会员 ID。自反表示元素关联自身，对称表示关系可反向，传递表示 xRy 且 yRz 推出 xRz。相等满足三者，有向依赖未必对称。</p>","If A={1,2}, B={2,3}, what is A−B?","A={1,2}、B={2,3}，A−B 是什么？","{1}; it is not the same as B−A={3}.","{1}，不同于 B−A={3}。"),
S("Functions and counting","函数与计数","<p>A function maps each domain element to exactly one codomain element. Injective means distinct inputs have distinct outputs; surjective means every codomain element is reached; bijective means both. If an ID-to-record function is injective, no two IDs map to the same record under that model. A pair of independent choices with a and b possibilities has a×b combinations. This counts configurations, not probabilities unless outcomes are equally likely. Mapping more than k objects into k buckets forces at least one shared bucket: the pigeonhole principle explains why hash collisions cannot always be avoided.</p>","<p>函数把定义域每个元素映射到值域中的唯一元素。单射要求不同输入对应不同输出，满射要求覆盖陪域，双射兼具两者。两个独立选择分别有 a、b 种可能时，共有 a×b 种组合；只有等可能时才能直接用于概率。超过 k 个对象放入 k 个桶，至少一个桶重复占用，这是鸽巢原理，也说明哈希碰撞无法总被避免。</p>","Can 5 distinct keys occupy 4 buckets without collision?","五个不同键放入四桶能不碰撞吗？","No, by the pigeonhole principle.","不能，由鸽巢原理。"),
S("Proof and induction","证明与归纳法","<p>A direct proof starts from assumptions and derives the claim. A counterexample disproves a universal statement. Induction proves a statement indexed by nonnegative integers: establish a base case, then prove that assuming it at k implies it at k+1. For 1+…+n=n(n+1)/2, n=0 gives zero. Add k+1 to k(k+1)/2 to obtain (k+1)(k+2)/2. Checking ten values is useful debugging but does not replace that step for infinitely many n. Loop invariants use a related initialisation-and-preservation structure.</p>","<p>直接证明从假设推出结论，反例否定全称陈述。归纳法先证明基础情况，再证明 k 成立推出 k+1 成立。对 1+…+n=n(n+1)/2，n=0 时为零；在 k(k+1)/2 上加 k+1 得 (k+1)(k+2)/2。检查十个值有助调试，却不能覆盖无限多个 n。循环不变式也采用初始化与保持结构。</p>","What must follow a base case in an induction proof?","归纳证明的基础情况之后需要什么？","An implication from the claim at k to the claim at k+1.","从 k 成立推出 k+1 成立。"),
S("Probability and expectation","概率与期望","<p>A finite sample space lists outcomes. For equally likely outcomes, P(A)=|A|/|Ω|. Conditional probability restricts attention to B: P(A|B)=P(A∩B)/P(B), requiring P(B)&gt;0. Independence means P(A∩B)=P(A)P(B); it is not the same as disjointness. Expected value weights values by probabilities. A fair die has expected value 3.5 even though no roll is 3.5. Linearity gives E[X+Y]=E[X]+E[Y] without requiring independence; other identities, such as multiplying expectations, do require additional assumptions.</p>","<p>有限样本空间列出结果。等可能时 P(A)=|A|/|Ω|。条件概率把范围限制为 B：P(A|B)=P(A∩B)/P(B)，要求 P(B)&gt;0。独立要求 P(A∩B)=P(A)P(B)，与互斥不同。期望按概率加权，公平骰子的期望为 3.5，但实际不会掷出 3.5。E[X+Y]=E[X]+E[Y] 无需独立，期望相乘等其他恒等式则需附加条件。</p>","Are disjoint events with positive probabilities independent?","概率非零的互斥事件独立吗？","No: their joint probability is zero but the product is positive.","不独立：联合概率为零，而概率乘积为正。")],
labs=[dict(file="m04_logic.py",title=P("Truth tables and sets","真值表与集合"),intro=P("Enumerate all four Boolean input pairs. The code checks implication against its contrapositive and verifies De Morgan's law.","枚举四种布尔输入，检查蕴含与逆否命题等价，并验证德摩根律。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Replace the contrapositive with q→p and find a counterexample.</li><li>Add symmetric difference for the sets.</li></ol>","<ol><li>改成 q→p 并找反例。</li><li>加入集合对称差。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>p=False, q=True makes p→q true but q→p false. Symmetric difference is {1,4}; it retains membership in exactly one set.</p>","<p>p 假、q 真时原命题真而逆命题假。对称差为 {1,4}，保留仅属于一方的元素。</p>")),dict(file="m04_probability.py",title=P("Exact probability and induction checks","精确概率与归纳检查"),intro=P("Two labelled dice have 36 equally likely ordered outcomes. Fractions avoids float approximation.","两枚有标记的骰子有 36 个等可能有序结果，Fractions 避免浮点近似。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Compute P(sum=8) and P(sum=8 | first=1).</li><li>Change the summation endpoint to exclude n; find a failing case.</li></ol>","<ol><li>计算和为 8 的概率，以及第一枚为 1 时的条件概率。</li><li>累加时排除 n，找失败案例。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>Five pairs total eight, giving 5/36. With the first die one, eight is impossible: zero. Excluding n breaks the formula already at n=1, because the computed sum becomes zero.</p>","<p>和为八有五种，概率 5/36；第一枚为一时不可能，概率零。排除 n 后，n=1 就失败，计算总和为零。</p>"))],
exercises=[E(1,"Negate a claim","否定陈述","Negate: every book has a unique ID.","否定：每本书都有唯一 ID。","<p>There exists a book that does not have a unique ID. Specify whether missing IDs count as invalid in the domain.</p>","<p>存在一本没有唯一 ID 的书。需说明定义域中缺失 ID 是否无效。</p>"),E(1,"Set calculation","集合计算","Compute union and intersection of {1,3} and {3,5}.","计算 {1,3} 与 {3,5} 的并交集。","<p>Union {1,3,5}; intersection {3}.</p>","<p>并集 {1,3,5}，交集 {3}。</p>"),E(2,"Converse","逆命题","Does p→q imply q→p? Give a counterexample.","p→q 能推出 q→p 吗？给反例。","<p>No. p=False, q=True satisfies p→q but violates q→p.</p>","<p>不能。p 假 q 真时前者真、后者假。</p>"),E(2,"Injectivity","单射性","Is f(x)=x² injective on integers? On nonnegative integers?","平方函数在整数上单射吗？非负整数呢？","<p>Not on integers: −2 and 2 both give 4. It is injective on nonnegative integers because larger nonnegative inputs have larger squares.</p>","<p>整数上不单射，−2 与 2 都给四；非负整数上单射，较大输入平方更大。</p>"),E(2,"Conditional chance","条件概率","For a fair die, compute P(even | greater than 3).","公平骰子大于三时为偶数的概率？","<p>The restricted outcomes are 4,5,6; two are even. Probability 2/3.</p>","<p>限制后结果为 4、5、6，两项偶数，概率 2/3。</p>"),E(3,"Induction","归纳法","Prove 0+…+n=n(n+1)/2.","证明 0+…+n=n(n+1)/2。","<p>Base n=0: both sides zero. Assume at k. Adding k+1 gives k(k+1)/2+(k+1)=(k+1)(k+2)/2, the claim for k+1.</p>","<p>基础 n=0 两边为零。假设 k 成立，加 k+1 得 k(k+1)/2+(k+1)=(k+1)(k+2)/2，故 k+1 成立。</p>"),E(2,"Expectation","期望","Find the expected number of heads in two fair coin flips.","两次公平抛硬币的正面数期望？","<p>Each indicator has expectation 1/2. Add them to get 1; alternatively weight counts 0,1,2 by 1/4,1/2,1/4.</p>","<p>每次指示变量期望 1/2，相加为一；也可按 1/4、1/2、1/4 加权 0、1、2。</p>"),E(3,"Relations","关系","Is 'has the same author as' an equivalence relation if every book has exactly one author?","每本书恰有一个作者时，同作者关系是等价关系吗？","<p>Yes: each book shares its author with itself; equality reverses; equal authors chain transitively. Missing or multiple authors require a revised relation.</p>","<p>是：自反、对称且作者相等可传递。缺失或多作者时需重新规定关系。</p>")],
quiz=[Q("A universal claim is disproved by?","什么推翻全称陈述？","One counterexample","一个反例","Ten confirming cases","十个成功案例","A faster machine","更快机器","Universal means every valid case.","全称要求所有有效情况。"),Q("A∩B means?","A∩B 是什么？","In both sets","同时属于双方","In either set","属于任一方","Only in A","仅在 A","Intersection retains shared membership.","交集保留共同成员。"),Q("Induction needs?","归纳需要什么？","Base and step","基础与归纳步骤","Only examples","仅例子","Only the conclusion","仅结论","The step extends the result beyond checked instances.","归纳步骤覆盖已检查实例之外。"),Q("A function assigns each input?","函数为每个输入分配什么？","Exactly one output","唯一输出","At least two outputs","至少两个输出","No output","没有输出","Its domain elements must each be mapped.","定义域每个元素都必须映射。"),Q("P(A|B) requires?","P(A|B) 要求什么？","P(B)>0","P(B)>0","A and B disjoint","A、B 互斥","P(A)=1","P(A)=1","We divide by P(B).","需要除以 P(B)。"),Q("A fair die's expected value?","公平骰子期望？","3.5","3.5","3","3","6","6","The mean is (1+…+6)/6.","均值为 (1+…+6)/6。")],
pitfalls=[P("The converse of an implication is not its contrapositive.","逆命题不同于逆否命题。"),P("Equally likely outcomes are an assumption, not automatic.","等可能是一项假设，并非自动成立。")],reading=[(P("MIT Mathematics for Computer Science","MIT 计算机科学数学"),"https://courses.csail.mit.edu/6.042/spring18/mcs.pdf",P("Read the opening proof and induction chapters; identify assumptions in one proof.","阅读开头的证明与归纳章节，指出一个证明的假设。"))],terms=[(P("Invariant","不变式"),P("A property preserved at specified execution points.","在指定执行位置保持的性质。")),(P("Conditional probability","条件概率"),P("Probability restricted to a condition with positive probability.","限制到正概率条件后的概率。")),(P("Bijection","双射"),P("A function both injective and surjective.","兼具单射与满射的函数。"))],review=P("<p>Explain why tests and proofs provide different evidence. Write one invariant for catalogue counting. Module 05 uses these tools to analyse search and sorting.</p>","<p>解释测试与证明提供的不同证据，为目录计数写一个不变式。模块 05 将分析搜索与排序。</p>")))
